# Names into addresses: the board connects to the network it keeps (wlan set in the console), gets an address by DHCP
# and asks the DNS server the router gave for the IPv4 address (the A record) of some names; it shows each with the
# time its answer took, then asks once more (the server has them in its cache now: its answers come faster). One name
# has a CNAME before its address (www.wikipedia.org), one does not exist (.invalid is never a real name). The same
# source for the ESP32, the ESP32-S3, the ESP32-C3, the ESP32-S31, the Pico W and the Pico 2 W: Asmonite translates it
# for the board of Project > Target, include "net.abel" takes the small IP stack of aBelle and the WiFi of that
# board from abelle\lib. Start it with F9, or upload it and type "dns" in the console; "dns asmonite.com" there asks
# for that name only.
#
# How a question looks (dns_lookup of net.abel): a UDP packet to port 53 with a number, the flag "recursion desired"
# and the name as labels ("example.com" is 7 example 3 com 0), type A, class IN. The answer has the same number and the
# question again, then its records: dns_lookup skips the ones that are no A record (a CNAME) and takes the first
# address.
include "console.abel"
include "net.abel"

NAMES = 5
found: char[4]

# the names to ask for, 0 .. NAMES - 1
def query_name(i) pchar:
    if i == 0:
        return "example.com"
    if i == 1:
        return "ptbtime1.ptb.de"
    if i == 2:
        return "www.wikipedia.org"
    if i == 3:
        return "asmonite.com"
    return "no-such-name.invalid"

# one name: "example.com = 172.66.147.243  (42 ms)"
def lookup(name: pchar):
    print(name)
    t0 = wifi_millis()
    ok = dns_lookup(name, found)
    t = wifi_millis() - t0
    if ok:
        print(" = ")
        print_ip(found)
    else:
        print(": no address")
    print("  (")
    print_int(t)
    println(" ms)")

def main():
    println("DNS")
    net_init()
    print("connecting to ")
    println(wifi_saved_name())
    r = wifi_connect_saved()
    if r != 0:
        print("wifi_connect: error ")
        print_int(r)
        print(" (")
        print(wifi_error_text(r))
        println(")")
        return
    if not dhcp_run():
        println("dhcp: no answer")
        return
    print("ip: ")
    print_ip(net_ip)
    print("  dns server: ")
    print_ip(net_dns)
    println("")
    a = args()
    while a[0] == ' ':
        a += 1
    if a[0] != 0:
        lookup(a)
    else:
        for i in 0..NAMES:
            lookup(query_name(i))
        println("once more:")
        for i in 0..NAMES:
            lookup(query_name(i))
    wifi_done()
    println("dns end")
